1
00:04:43,636 --> 00:04:49,636
As darkness falls, the last dragon will choose its rider.

2
00:09:27,272 --> 00:09:33,272
Eragon is a fantasy, action, adventure film directed by Stefen Fangmeier.

3
00:14:10,909 --> 00:14:16,909
In his homeland of Alagaesia, a farm boy happens upon a dragon's egg -- a discovery that leads him on a
predestined journey where he realized he's the one person who can defend his home against an evil king.

4
00:18:54,545 --> 00:19:00,545
Eragon, played by Ed Speleers.

5
00:23:38,181 --> 00:23:44,181
Brom, played by Jeremy Irons.

6
00:28:21,818 --> 00:28:27,818
Arya, played by Sienna Guillory.

7
00:33:05,454 --> 00:33:11,454
Durza, played by Robert Carlyle.

8
00:37:49,090 --> 00:37:55,090
King Galbatorix, played by John Malkovich.

9
00:42:32,727 --> 00:42:38,727
Murtagh, played by Garrett Hedlund.

10
00:47:16,363 --> 00:47:22,363
Eragon (stylized in all lowercase) is a 2006 fantasy adventure film directed by Stefen Fangmeier (in his directorial
debut) and written by Peter Buchman, loosely based on Christopher Paolini's 2002 novel of the same name.

11
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
It stars Ed Speleers in the title role as well as Jeremy Irons, Sienna Guillory, Robert Carlyle, Djimon
Hounsou, Garrett Hedlund, Joss Stone, and John Malkovich, with Rachel Weisz as Saphira the dragon.

12
00:56:43,636 --> 00:56:49,636
The film also marked the film debuts for Speleers and Stone.

13
01:01:27,272 --> 01:01:33,272
Principal photography took place at the Mafilm Fót Studios
in Hungary, starting on August 1, 2005.

14
01:06:10,909 --> 01:06:16,909
Visual effects and animation were provided by Industrial
Light & Magic, Weta Digital and Cinesite.

15
01:10:54,545 --> 01:11:00,545
Eragon was released worldwide on December 15, 2006, by 20th Century Fox.

16
01:15:38,181 --> 01:15:44,181
It received widespread negative reviews from critics and book fans, who criticized its acting, screenplay, visuals and
unfaithfulness to the source material, though its CGI and the performances of Speleers and Irons were praised by a few critics.

17
01:20:21,818 --> 01:20:27,818
It was the 10th worst reviewed film of 2006 on Rotten Tomatoes, but
the 31st highest-grossing film of 2006 in the US.

18
01:25:05,454 --> 01:25:11,454
The film was released for home entertainment on March 20, 2007.

19
01:29:49,090 --> 01:29:55,090
Originally, Eragon was supposed to be the first in a franchise based on Paolini's Inheritance
Cycle book series, with Fangmeirer shooting both Eldest and Brisingr back-to-back.

20
01:34:32,727 --> 01:34:38,727
However, following the poor critical reception of Eragon on its release, and its
box-office performance,  the planned sequels were not produced.

21
01:39:16,363 --> 01:39:22,363
The film explores themes of princess, based on
novel or book, elves, magic, kingdom.
